{
  "abstract": "Lean 4 formalization of sensitivity-versus-real-degree bounds for Boolean functions f : {0, 1}^n -> {0, 1}, motivated by Terence Tao's Optimization Constant #37a. Establishes exact real polynomial degree via Boolean-lattice Mobius inversion, explicit kernel-verified witnesses (3, 2, 3), (6, 3, 6), (9, 4, 9), and (13, 5, 13), the asymptotic lower bound log 6 / log 3 <= degSensitivityExponent via iterated composition and the Chebyshev cubic upper bound, exact sharp bounds B_2 = 3, B_3 = 6, a zero-search 10-line elementary algebraic proof of B_4 = 9, and sharpened low-degree upper bounds B_5 <= 14, B_6 <= 20, B_7 <= 28, B_8 <= 36, and B_9 <= 46 strictly improving the univariate symmetrisation LP bounds of Wellens (2022) via pure-integer Terwilliger LP/PSD certificates, sum-of-squares rigidity, and forbidden-subgraph arguments. These fixed-degree bounds do not alter the known bounds [log_3 6, 2] on either the asymptotic uniform-big-O exponent `degSensitivityExponent` or Tao's distinct finite-supremum constant `C_37`.",
